From c2e6c2a7be06751469e31b86a1911b508899681d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:31:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] provisiondb: Look up the default database in
 PKGDATADIR
To: ofono@lists.linux.dev

provision_db_new_default() only tries the hard-coded path
/usr/share/ofono/provision.db, while the build installs the database to
$(pkgdatadir), i.e. ${datadir}/ofono. With any prefix other than /usr
(the autoconf default /usr/local, or distributions such as NixOS that
install every package into its own prefix) the database is never found,
and oFono logs "Unable to open provisioning database!" and fails to
provision any GPRS context automatically.

Use the configured PKGDATADIR instead. For the usual --prefix=/usr build
the path is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/provisiondb.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/provisiondb.c b/src/provisiondb.c
index 6a913d8..39ec417 100644
--- a/src/provisiondb.c
+++ b/src/provisiondb.c
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@ struct provision_db *provision_db_new_default(void)
 {
 	struct provision_db *db = NULL;
 	size_t i;
-	const char * const paths[] = { "/usr/share/ofono/provision.db" };
+	const char * const paths[] = { PKGDATADIR "/provision.db" };
 
 	for (i = 0; !db && i < L_ARRAY_SIZE(paths); i++)
 		db = provision_db_new(paths[i]);
